1|# Database Operations
2|
3|- Every we do database operations, using the backend class, it needs to be always wrapped in an try catch block, and we need to log the error.
4|
5|```php
6|$utilisationBuyer = new UtilisationBuyer();
7|$utilisationBuyer->load([UtilisationBuyer::UTILISATION_ID => $this->utilisation->getUtilisationId()]);
8|try {
9|    $utilisationBuyer->setBuyerId($this->buyerId);
10|    $utilisationBuyer->setUtilisationId($this->utilisation->getUtilisationId());
11|    $utilisationBuyer->save();
12|} catch (Exception $exception) {
13|    ErrorHandler::trigger($exception->getMessage(), E_USER_NOTICE);
14|}
15|```
16|
17|# Paid Options
18|
19|- Every time you need to check if the paid option is enabled you need to use this format.
20|
21|```php
22|$paidOptions = new PaidOptions();
23|if ($paidOptions->existEntry(PaidOptions::PAID_OPTION)) {
24|}
25|```
26|
27|# Administration Modules
28|
29|- When adding a new Administration module, do not assume the DB/navigation records are enough to show it on the Administration landing page.
30|- The direct URL can work while the module is still missing from the Administration grid.
31|- Add the module route/rights in the database scripts as usual:
32|  - `module`
33|  - `modules`
34|  - `menu_to_module`
35|  - `navigation`
36|  - permission/right group inserts needed for the target users
37|- Add or reuse a submenu constant in `fcm/Variables/FCM_Setting.php` for the `a2` module number.
38|- Add a helper method in `fcm/Frontend/Home/Home.php` following the existing `do...()` pattern:
39|
40|```php
41|protected function doExampleManagement(): void
42|{
43|    if (! $this->hasModule('ExampleManagement')) {
44|        return;
45|    }
46|
47|    $this->mainurl->addParameter(url::A1, FCM_Setting::TOPMENU_ADMIN);
48|    $this->mainurl->addParameter(url::A2, FCM_Setting::SUBMENU_EXAMPLE_MANAGEMENT);
49|    $this->mainurl->addParameter(ActionForm::$RESET_TAG, 1);
50|    $this->create_Tr_HomeSub($this->mainurl, Icons::COGS, $this->getTranslation('exampleManagement'), $this->column);
51|    $this->mainurl->removeParameters();
52|}
53|```
54|
55|- Call that helper from the correct column method in `fcm/Frontend/Administration.php`, for example `prepareThirdColumn()` for entries under `Other`.
56|- Validate both paths:
57|  - Open the direct URL, for example `a1=98&a2=<module-number>`.
58|  - Open Administration and confirm the tile appears in the expected section for a user with the module permission.
59|
60|# Rules
61|
62|- In DataIntegration, always wrap `json_encode()` and `json_decode()` in a local `try/catch` and handle `JsonException` explicitly instead of calling them bare.
63|- We want the minimal production ready viable solution so do not do crazy abstractions

